"blurb": "Feminine nouns in -α and -η, the learned type η πόλη / οι πόλεις, feminines in -ος, the -δες plurals of γιαγιά and αλεπού, and the tricky genitive plural.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Feminine nouns are the easiest Greek nouns: most end in **-α** or **-η**, they keep that vowel through the singular, add **-ς** only in the genitive, and take **-ες** in the plural. The only real trap is the genitive plural, where the stress often jumps to the end."
